   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 402 of the laws of 1994, amending the state\nadministrative procedure act relating to requiring certain agencies to submit\nregulatory agendas for publication in the state register, in relation to the\neffectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S9394",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S9394-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2, Chap 402 of 1994",
    "lawSection": "State",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9394\n\nSPONSOR: RYAN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 402 of the laws of 1994, amending the state\nadministrative procedure act relating to requiring certain agencies to\nsubmit regulatory agendas for publication in the state register, in\nrelation to the effectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nExtends certain provisions of the state administrative procedure act\nrelating to requiring certain agencies to submit regulatory agendas for\npublication in the state register\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 2 extends the expiration date of the existing law from December\n31, 2024 to December 31, 2028.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill extends section 202-d of the State Administrative Procedures\nAct which requires departments of health, education, environmental\nconservation, financial services, labor, agriculture and markets, motor\nvehicles and state, the offices of children and family services and\ntemporary and disability assistance, the division of housing and commu-\nnity renewal, the state gaming commission, the office of mental health,\nthe office for people with developmental disabilities and the workers'\ncompensation board, and any other department or agency specified by the\ngovernor or his or her designee to submit their regulatory agendas for\npublication in the State Register.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nLast extended for 4 years in section 1 of item FFF of subpart B of part\nXXX of chapter 58 of the laws of 2020\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
